This directory contains all the IDL routines and data files
needed to reproduce the main results in the H0DN paper.

The main workhorse is the routine in org_v3p9.pro , called org_v3p9.
This reflects V3.9, which has been slightly cleaned up compared to 
versions V3.7 and V3.8 used during production; however, the results
have been tested to be identical.  Additional user-callable routines include
vars.pro, which produces all the main variants in Table 4 of the paper
(and a few extra), and the utilities avclip.pro, mpinv.pro,
and uniquify.pro, used by the main routine.  Other routines
are primarily designed to be called from org_v3p9 or vars.

To improve readability, detailed information on how the routines work,
how the data files are defined, and so on has been split into several
README, which are numbered in logical order.
This readme only includes basic information about the program.

For a quick result, save the data in the directory ../data,
as recommended in the installation instructions.  Then run from 
the IDL prompt the following command:

vars, basedir='../data/', outdir='./output/', save='savefile.sav'

This will run all the variants in Table 4 of the paper (except for the O
variants, which come from a different process), provide on-screen
summary of results, create text and postscript files for each in the
directory ./output (which must be created beforehand), and save
relevant output in the IDL save file 'savefile.sav'.  (If the data
have been saved in the current directory, simply leave out the
basedir parameter.)

More details on the interpretation of the output files
wll be provided in README_IDL_5_OUTPUT.

For specific cases, extract the relevant org_v3p9
command from vars.pro (a short descriptrion is
provided for each instance) and run it standalone;
for example, the command for V02 (baseline plus MIRAs) is:

basedir = '../data/'
id = 'V02'
outdir = './'
label = id + ': Baseline + Miras'
org_v3p9, config='none', anchor_data='anchors.dat', basedir=basedir, $
          details=dd, /sbf_calib, groups_file='groups.dat', /mm, $
          sn1a_calib='sn1a_calib.dat', sn1a_hf='sn1a_hf_pp.dat', $
          sn1a_covar='sn1a_covar_pp.dat', $
          exclude_list=['SMC','*jagb*','b25'], $
          log=outdir+id+'.txt', plot=outdir+id+'.ps', $
          plabel=label

Here ID and LABEL are used to name the output text and plot files,
with OUTDIR as  their location.  The parameters in the org_v3p9 call
have the following meaning:

config='none'                        Do not use a configuration file
anchor_data='anchors.dat'            Anchor name and uncertainties
basedir=basedir                      The default location for data files
details=dd                           Output structure with solution details
/sbf_calib                           Include SBF data with default files
groups_file='groups.dat'             Use the GROUPS file named
/mm                                  Include megamasers with the default files
sn1a_calib='sn1a_calib.dat'          Include SN1A calibrators in named file
sn1a_hf='sn1a_hf_pp.dat'             Include SN1A in Hubble flow from named file (Pantheon+)
sn1a_covar='sn1a_covar_pp.dat'       Covariance for SN1a in Hubble flow from named file (Pantheon+)
exclude_list=['SMC','*jagb*','b25']  Exclude list for host measurements
log=outdir+id+'.txt'                 File with summary output
plot=outdir+id+'.ps'                 File with diagnostic plot (in postscript format)
plabel=label                         Label used in plot

More details on input parameters and output variables are given
in the specific README files.

